<ns0:exercise xmlns:ns0="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:ns1="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" id="fs-id1167825884747" class="material-set-2">
<ns0:problem id="fs-id1167825884749">
<ns0:para id="fs-id1167825884751">Every day a new puzzle is downloaded into Ken’s account. Right now he has 43 puzzles in his account. The function <ns1:math><ns1:mrow><ns1:mi>N</ns1:mi><ns1:mrow><ns1:mo>(</ns1:mo><ns1:mi>t</ns1:mi><ns1:mo>)</ns1:mo></ns1:mrow><ns1:mo>=</ns1:mo><ns1:mn>43</ns1:mn><ns1:mo>+</ns1:mo><ns1:mi>t</ns1:mi></ns1:mrow></ns1:math> represents the relation between the number of puzzles, <ns0:emphasis effect="italics">N</ns0:emphasis>, and the time, <ns0:emphasis effect="italics">t</ns0:emphasis>, measured in days.</ns0:para>
<ns0:para id="fs-id1167829620296"><ns0:span class="token">ⓐ</ns0:span> Determine the independent and dependent variable.</ns0:para>
<ns0:para id="fs-id1167829620303"><ns0:span class="token">ⓑ</ns0:span> Find <ns1:math><ns1:mrow><ns1:mi>N</ns1:mi><ns1:mrow><ns1:mo>(</ns1:mo><ns1:mrow><ns1:mn>30</ns1:mn></ns1:mrow><ns1:mo>)</ns1:mo></ns1:mrow><ns1:mo>.</ns1:mo></ns1:mrow></ns1:math> Explain what this result means.</ns0:para>
</ns0:problem>
</ns0:exercise>
